        "answer": {
          "short": "B",
          "worked": "A: $\\$325$ is the median for people under 21 and the lower quartile for people 21 years and older. Approximately $50\\%$ and $75\\%$, respectively, earned more than this amount, so A is false.\n\nB: $\\$350$ is the upper quartile for people under 21. Approximately $75\\%$ earned less than this amount, so B is true.\n\nC: $\\$350$ is the upper quartile for people 21 years and older. Approximately $25\\%$ earned more than this amount, so C is false.\n\nD: For people under 21, $\\$325$ to $\\$350$ runs from the median to the upper quartile and contains approximately $25\\%$ of the group, so D is false.\n\nCorrect answer: B.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
